{"id": "7ee46b1f-217d-40c6-ace0-2539b9f0f661", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I'm noting the key facts about GetEstimatedCarbonEmissions: it covers 14 months of monthly, paginated data, with separate calls grouped by SERVICE/REGION and by USAGE_ACCOUNT_ID, where multiple accounts returned signals a management-account view. Only EC2, S3, and CloudFront get broken out individually (everything else falls under "Other"), and since data for month M publishes by the 21st of M+1, the latest available month could be two months back before that date.

I should check the emissions-api-reference.md and emissions-collection.md docs for more detail on granularity, current-month data availability, and the member account view.

"}]}
